hi there i'm lottie winter the beauty  editor of glamour uk  today i'm going to be trying botox and  for my procedure  i'm going to go and visit dr michael  prager  i've tried botox before but any  treatment should start with a  consultation ask your doctor if there's  any aftercare that you need to do  or anything that you may need to be  aware of after your treatment is  finished  botox is actually a muscle relaxant so  that's how it was discovered  and the cosmetic side effect was just a  byproduct  of the muscle relaxation effect i  grind my teeth at night really really  badly and it results in a lot of neck  pain and headaches so  botox can really help with that and also  help relieve migraines through frowning  and stress  but also obviously as a kind of  preventative aging  process for me that's also another  benefit  the botox is admittedly a poison but  it's injected in a minute amount into  the muscle it takes  a couple of days and then the muscle  relaxing effect kicks in  okay so it was a little bit painful but  only at the exact  moment the needle went in as soon as the  injection  was finished i didn't feel any pain  i am quite particular when i choose my  practitioner for cosmetic treatments i  always want to see  a qualified doctor i also always go to a  clinical setting  i know that sometimes you can go and  have  you know botox treatments at home or  kind of in a traveling clinic  i don't do that because i think that  knowing someone's  address the clinic address adds a layer  of accountability  so that if something goes wrong you know  exactly where you can go  how do you choose your botox  practitioner  i think make sure that he's not one of  the practitioners that give the people  what they want  i think the worst approach and the worst  patient is the one that tells the  practitioner what to do botox is  expensive the actual substance is  expensive so  you should be careful by looking at the  price tag because  basically it means you either get  shortchanged or you get something else  or  it's possibly not a great not as great a  deal as it seems  the treatment i received was 895  pounds obviously that depends on  which clinic you go to and how many  areas you get treated  so i had my forehead and my jaw but i  know that  dr prager likes to treat the face as a  whole  so that everything looks really balanced  so this is the final result it takes  around three days to a week  to get the full effect i had the  treatment maybe  two or three weeks ago now so it's the  same thing that i have done every single  time and every single time the results  are the same so i know what to expect  i didn't get any bruising although i  suspect that with any kind of injectable  treatment  that is a possibility and if i was going  to  tell my friends about this treatment um  i would tell them honestly that yeah  it's a little painful when it's  happening but  in my experience i haven't had any  negative effects  the things i find most beautiful are  when someone is confident and happy  for me there is a lot of beauty in  revealing your true self  whether that be embracing how you look  or your body or  your personality share your stories and  ask as many questions as you like in the  comments
 

